--- Abuja Federal Capital Territory / Municipal Area Council [None] P36=None
    en: 'Abuja' rev 1376903060 2026-09-26T22:05:00Z: {}
      lead: '''Abuja''' () is the capital city of [[Nigeria]], strategically situated at the geographic midpoint of the country within the [[Federal Capital Territory (Nigeria)|Federal Capital Territory]] (FCT).
      lead: As the seat of the [[Federal Government of Nigeria]], it hosts key national institutions, landmarks, and buildings spread across its over 50 districts.
      lead: It replaced [[Lagos]] (the most populous city in Nigeria) as the capital on 12 December 1991.
      lead: Abuja is known for being one of the few purpose-built capital cities in Africa, as well as being one of the wealthiest.
      lead: Abuja is Nigeria's [[Administration (government)|administrative]] and political capital.
      lead: It is also a key capital on the African continent due to Nigeria's [[geo-political|geopolitical]] influence in regional affairs.
    fr: None -- no article
